### agentry-unsafe-kali

    Base:       kalilinux/kali-rolling, by digest (images.tsv, agentry-kali-rolling)
    Context:    build/agentry-unsafe-kali/
    Our image:  agentry-unsafe-kali

A Kali Linux base with Debian and Kali packages installed from Kali's archive
(`ca-certificates`, `python3`, `python3-venv` and what they depend on), each
under its own licence as recorded in `/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright`
inside the image. What we add is ours, under MIT: the command index and the
list of ambiguous commands under `/etc/agentry/unsafe/`, which are generated
from Kali's published `Contents` and `Packages` indexes, and the extras list.
The image installs no tool the extras list names; the CLI installs those per
QuickAgent, from Kali's archive and PyPI, under their own licences. Kali Linux
is a trademark of OffSec Services Limited, used here only to identify the
upstream distribution; nothing built here is a Kali or OffSec product.

